well, after what? 18 months of solid nethack addiction? its time to
write up my first acension post. started nethack as unspoiled as i
could until these last few months: got a few characters to the castle
and one or two beyond it. Gehennemon made my head spin, so i read up
on just what the hell you're expected to do down there. ended up
reading a little more than i wouldve like, but no bother!  Dent was my
first character to have ever done the invocation. my other characters,
mostly wizards and archs, have always fallen pray to a SD while trying
to get things "just right" before going for the amulet.

just pulled an all-nighter, started Dent two days ago and played every
night. lets see what i can remember....

Setting off on his treasure hunt, Dent the Digger didnt bring anything
out of the ordinary beyond his lucky hat and a small, friendly dog.
Dent was fond of his whip and with the help of his lil friend, he
fended off the creatures of the dungeon using his quickness to keep
out of harms way. There were two large general stores early on, the
shopkeeps drove a hard bargain, but lucky for Dent, he'd tunneled his
way into several hidden rooms filled with gold. He used to gold to by
some fancy leather armor, some very useful mystic parchments, and a
pair of gloves that didnt seem to do much, but cost an awful lot. No
bother, by the fourth level there was a stair shaft that led to
cavernous mines, lit like the rooms of the dungeon above!

The trip down the mines went pretty smoothly, Dent thought. Some dog
treats he'd bought above won him the loyalty of another dog, though
his pets didnt get along to well with the fellows in the mine. As a
result Dent had his pack full of valuable accessories, and to his
bemusement, there was a town in the middle of these mine caves.
"Surely, this must be a Gnome-Town!" he laughed. The town wasnt very
hospitable though, dark and confusing. And after poking around some, a
villanous watch-captain with some flashy silver sword slew one of his
friendly dogs! C'mon, it was _obvious_ those dwarves started it! Well,
me and my other dog, my whip and this magic trick will play a nasty
trick on him! Will lock the rest of his men out of our way... then...
whirr-snapp! *yank* "Hey!" Dent's dog attacked, then the magic trick
put the pushy Captain into a dazed slumber. And thus Dent became a
force the dungeon would learn to reckon with. His Silver Swords, loyal
companions and potent magic would earn him immortality yet!

heheh, ok at any rate found two magic harps in gnome-town... hmmm,
wouldve prefered a BoH and a marker, but ok. bought some protection,
got a silver sword and headed back to the main line.

sokoban gave me an amulet. i had tamed a pony, who became a very
hungry warhorse. on the last level of sokoban, horse bit dog then
starved. there were a couple of altars between the mines and
sokoban... and i cant remember if i got Werebane before or after
clearing the mines, but it was my first gift. Using one of those magic
harps, i tamed a baby silver dragon... formerly a gnome lord who'd
jump on a poly trap. with his help i got my luckstone, and with my
help he grew up to be a full size silver dragon. an unfortunate
accident with another poly trap fortuntately left me feeling much more
feminine and nothing got torn up.

At this point the other good things i had going for me were great
low-level spell finds. sleep, force bolt, light, and healing. Armor
wasnt anything extra ordinary, and hadnt found any ?oEA. my best piece
was a +2 studded. After i'd bought some protection, me and Silver had
taken out the priest in gnome town, and i wore his robe. its tough to
remember the exact sequence of events here...

Around DL18 i found a real Archaelogical gold mine, an abandoned
temple filled with the belongings of some lunatic wizard. a full kit
was there more or less(+3[HoB, +2[BoS, +4[SDSM, +4[T-Shirt : "Dont
Panic!" perfect!), as well as countless other useful items. A potion
shop buried deep in the dungeon sold me a smoky potion of gain ability
that i blessed. out popped a djinn for my first wish... blessed
greased bag of holding please.

At this point there were two things that i really wanted: Grayswandir
and the Eye of Aetheopica. The Eye was on the wizard, i was 80% sure
he was neutral, so i considered trying to change alignment, but the
quest first! i hacked my way to XL14 then quaffed a potion for XL15.
Got the Orb without commotion. Well, i know create monster, i have a
couple wands, i'm now XL17, lets sac for Grayswandir, i'll get it
since im lawful. Man, I wouldve killed for the Eye... only 75-100 Pw,
i sacrificed for... five artifacts? the fifth was finally Grayswandir.
I nearly gave up, but on an altar a little ways down i tried another
go at it, and got it.

no ludious, cleared the castle. That wizard cache had a bunch of great
spells, Ident, Poly, magic missle, etc... starting with wands of poly
i made a ton of scrolls to enchant out my weapons and gloves of dex. I
dont know any alchemy beyond poly-piling and quaffing, but by the time
i was ready to delve gehennemon i was ~XL24 with ~450HP and ~200PW.
*shrug* who needs the Eye?  Who needs a wand of wishing? wished for a
marker anyway, hadnt found any, and those at the wizard's grave were
dried out, wrote some genocide and cursed them. Sent in some nurses.
Then some tengus (only had TC with a ring)

My silver dragon had been turned to stone, then i had a black dragon
turned to stone. but i like riding dragons, my third black dragon was
a keeper, he made it all the way to the first plane... *sigh* Anyway,
Hell was tedious. I used another wish for a second blessed bag of
holding, named it library and kept some spellbooks in it, lugged it
downstairs every few levels. Vlads Tower got interesting... Vlad read
a scroll of teleportation. And disappeared. He wasnt in his tower. He
wasnt anywhere in Gehennemon. I had to hunt him down, and finally
found him on DL8 or 9. heheh, well, if i were in his shoes, seeing
those two silver swords climbing up his ladder, i'd be wishing for a
c?oTele too.

By the time i rode my dragon into the the Wizard's Tower i'd quaffed
enough potions of Gain Level to have been XL45. HP was over 600, Power
was over three. Damn, whats the order you have to use these things in?
lit the candles first, so far so good. rang the bell next? then read
the book. it worked! Having the amulet was strange, i've read about it
throwing you back, but it only threw me down one level, the other
times it just put me somewhere else on the current. The wizard came
back twice before the planes...

The planes were weirder than i expected. Earth started out rough, the
wizard showed up immediately and between him and an arch-lich, had
summoned up a mess of heavies. My dragon didnt make it out. I had read
about the magic portals and used my orb to find it. I didnt need to on
the others. Air was confusing, didnt get the idea that i had to
levitate right away. The portal was on the opposite side, saw some
monsters stumble across it.  Water was even stranger, wasnt really
sure what the hell was going on, where'd that boulder come from? heh.
but before i had to get the hang of what was going on, i was on
fire... or was fire first? fire was the most straight forward,
levitated across the lava, saw something fall into the portal, hacked
up some elementals and dove in. Lastly, astral was all locust, a
plague of biblical proportions. went left first, waded through ants up
to my elbows. But left was neutral, so i had to wade back out. Maybe
up the middle? used my swords almost exclusively, with a few zaps of
death for good measure, and the middle was Quetzalcoatl!

i wish i had that dump patch i've heard people talk about...

